docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:17: trailing whitespace.
+## Global Decisions
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:18: trailing whitespace.
+
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:19: trailing whitespace.
+- V1 operator identity is a string derived from admin headers:
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:20: trailing whitespace.
+  - `x-operator-id` if present and non-empty.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:21: trailing whitespace.
+  - `admin-secret` when the header is absent.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:22: trailing whitespace.
+  - `x-operator-label` if present and non-empty.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:23: trailing whitespace.
+  - `Admin operator` when the label header is absent.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:24: trailing whitespace.
+- Missing `creator_review_statuses` rows are projected as `{ status: "needs_review", riskLevel: "unknown" }`.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:25: trailing whitespace.
+- Public and creator-facing routes do not read the new operator CRM tables.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:26: trailing whitespace.
+- Flagged creators are visible in the global review queue, hidden by default when a queue is opened with `mission_id`, and visible there only when `status=flagged` is requested.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:27: trailing whitespace.
+- Shortlisting a flagged creator requires a non-empty note.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:28: trailing whitespace.
+- Moving a flagged creator to `invited` returns `409` until the creator is moved out of `flagged`.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-operator-creator-selection-crm.md:29: trailing whitespace.
+- API responses use snake_case for nested database-like fields already used by admin routes (`creator_review`, `mission_shortlist`) and camelCase inside new frontend-only types.
