+## 1. Purpose
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-adfocate-mission-completion-reward-handoff-design.md:12: trailing whitespace.
+
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-adfocate-mission-completion-reward-handoff-design.md:13: trailing whitespace.
+This phase closes the operational gap between verified publication proof and financial processing.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-adfocate-mission-completion-reward-handoff-design.md:14: trailing whitespace.
+
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-adfocate-mission-completion-reward-handoff-design.md:15: trailing whitespace.
+An authorized operator can confirm that an active-workspace mission is complete only when every required publication item has verified proof. Adfocate then freezes the reward contract and workspace processing SLA, records an auditable completion decision, advances the active-mission workflow to `reward_pending`, and creates a durable finance handoff.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-adfocate-mission-completion-reward-handoff-design.md:16: trailing whitespace.
+
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-adfocate-mission-completion-reward-handoff-design.md:17: trailing whitespace.
+This phase does not issue rewards. It does not credit points, cash, earnings, or XP; mutate workspace budgets; approve the legacy mission submission; or implement withdrawal and payout. Its purpose is to create a trustworthy, reviewable boundary between content verification and later financial issuance.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-adfocate-mission-completion-reward-handoff-design.md:18: trailing whitespace.
+
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-adfocate-mission-completion-reward-handoff-design.md:19: trailing whitespace.
+## 2. Approved Product Decisions
